VVEERRSSIIOONNSS
       The glibc implementation of pptthhrreeaadd__kkiillll() gives an error (EEIINNVVAALL) on
       attempts to send either of the real‐time signals used internally by the
       NPTL threading implementation.  See nnppttll(7) for details.

       POSIX.1‐2008 recommends that if an implementation detects the use of a
       thread ID after the end of its lifetime, pptthhrreeaadd__kkiillll() should return
       the error EESSRRCCHH.  The glibc implementation returns this error in the
       cases where an invalid thread ID can be detected.  But note also that
       POSIX says that an attempt to use a thread ID whose lifetime has ended
       produces undefined behavior, and an attempt to use an invalid thread ID
       in a call to pptthhrreeaadd__kkiillll() can, for example, cause a segmentation
       fault.

